<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The process begins immediately upon the vehicle's exit from the transport carrier, under optimal daylight conditions.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This specific timing is critical to avoid shadows or artificial lighting that may obscure surface defects.</span></li></ul>
<p>The agent must conduct a comprehensive re-inspection of the vehicle, systematically comparing its current physical state against the high-resolution photographs captured during the initial pickup. This visual audit covers critical components including the fairings, mirrors, wheels, tires, and chrome elements, ensuring that no new scratches, dents, or mechanical issues have occurred during transit.</p>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Lighting Requirement:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Perform the inspection exclusively during daylight hours to guarantee accurate color and texture visibility for all exterior panels.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Photo Comparison:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Cross-reference every major body panel and accessory against the digital documentation from the pickup phase to identify any discrepancies.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Functional Check:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Briefly verify that all lights, signals, and the horn are operational to confirm the vehicle remains in a usable condition.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<p>Following the visual inspection, the agent must proceed with odometer verification. The current mileage displayed on the dashboard must be meticulously cross-checked against the figures recorded in the Legal Representative (LR) bilty. Any variance exceeding the standard tolerance range must be flagged immediately, as this could indicate unauthorized usage or tampering during the transit period.</p>
<p>This step is essential for maintaining the integrity of the vehicle's usage history and validating the scope of the transport service provided. Once the physical condition and mileage data are confirmed as consistent with the documentation, the final step involves the signed condition sign-off.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Odometer Audit:</strong> Match the live dashboard reading precisely with the entry in the LR bilty to validate transit integrity.</li>
<li><strong>Discrepancy Resolution:</strong> If any mismatch is found, halt the handover and document the issue before proceeding.</li>
<li><strong>Final Sign-Off:</strong> The recipient must sign the condition report, explicitly acknowledging that the vehicle has been received in the state described in the report.</li>
<li><strong>Document Retention:</strong> Both the agent and the recipient should retain copies of the signed document for future reference or dispute resolution.</li>
</ul>
<p>This structured approach minimizes liability risks and ensures a seamless transition of ownership back to the customer. By adhering to strict daylight inspection protocols and rigorous document verification, the logistics provider demonstrates a commitment to vehicle safety and customer satisfaction.</p>
<p>The signed sign-off serves as the legal closure of the transport contract, marking the end of the carrier's responsibility for the vehicle's condition. Consistency in this final step is paramount for maintaining trust and operational efficiency within the two-wheeler logistics network.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



